cellPad: the keyboard fallback on macOS, and through SDL elsewhere.

The toolkit's keyboard fallback for port 0 is Windows-only (GetAsyncKeyState). The key table is now the same on every host
(arrows, Z/X/A/S = cross/circle/square/triangle, Q/W = L1/R1, 1/2 = L2/R2, Return = start, Tab = select) over a per-host
pad_key_down: CGEventSourceKeyState on macOS (needs no event tap or window; "focused" is NSApplication.isActive, asked
through the Objective-C runtime so the file stays plain C), SDL scancodes on Linux and Windows. The XInput block moves after
the keyboard code so the keyboard compiles without XInput.

Upstream: not proposed.
